<h3 id=3D"heading-1-what-is-cli-and-gui" class=3D"g-md-h3 gamut-t98mq7-Styl=
edText e8i0p5k0">1. What is CLI and GUI?</h3>
<p class=3D"g-md-p">A CLI (Command Line Interface) is a text-based interfac=
e where users type commands to interact with the system. A GUI (Graphical U=
ser Interface), on the other hand, allows users to interact through visual =
elements like buttons, icons, and windows. CLI is faster and more powerful =
for advanced users, while GUI is more user-friendly for beginners. </p>
<h3 id=3D"heading-2-is-cli-a-programming-language" class=3D"g-md-h3 gamut-t=
98mq7-StyledText e8i0p5k0">2. Is CLI a programming language?</h3>
<p class=3D"g-md-p">No, CLI is not a <a data-testid=3D"domain-agnostic-link=
" href=3D"https://www.AI Academy by RiWoT.com/article/what-is-programming" target=3D=
"_blank" class=3D"gamut-1r92bn9-AnchorBase e14vpv2g0">programming</a> langu=
age. It=E2=80=99s an interface that allows users to interact with the opera=
ting system using command syntax. However, through the CLI, you can run scr=
ipts and commands written in scripting languages like Bash, Python, or Powe=
rShell. </p>
<h3 id=3D"heading-3-what-is-bash-and-why-is-it-used" class=3D"g-md-h3 gamut=
-t98mq7-StyledText e8i0p5k0">3. What is Bash, and why is it used?</h3>
<p class=3D"g-md-p">Bash stands for Bourne Again Shell and is a popular Uni=
x shell and command language. It=E2=80=99s used for navigating the file sys=
tem, running programs, and automating tasks using shell scripts. It=E2=80=
=99s widely used on macOS, Linux, and in tools like Git Bash for Windows. <=
/p>
<h3 id=3D"heading-4-whats-the-difference-between-bash-and-command-prompt" c=
lass=3D"g-md-h3 gamut-t98mq7-StyledText e8i0p5k0">4. What=E2=80=99s the dif=
ference between Bash and Command Prompt?</h3>
<p class=3D"g-md-p">Bash is commonly used on Unix-based systems like Linux =
and macOS, while Command Prompt is the default CLI for Windows. Bash offers=
 more powerful scripting capabilities and is favored by developers for auto=
mation and working with tools like Git. Command Prompt is more limited in c=
omparison. </p>
<h3 id=3D"heading-5-do-i-need-to-know-cli-to-use-git" class=3D"g-md-h3 gamu=
t-t98mq7-StyledText e8i0p5k0">5. Do I need to know CLI to use Git?</h3>
<p class=3D"g-md-p">Yes, a basic understanding of the Command Line Interfac=
e is helpful for using Git effectively. Most Git workflows like cloning rep=
ositories, committing changes, or pushing code are commonly done via CLI to=
ols such as Git Bash.</p>
